  <main>
    <h1 class="title">CADENT, 2026</h1>
    <p>Most days hold a few things you mean to repeat: a walk after lunch, a page of reading, water for the plants. You schedule them. A phone reminder competes with everything else on the phone and gets swiped away. Following through depends on the distance between that schedule and the person it belongs to.</p>
    <p>Cadent is a small robot that lives in the home and closes that distance. It is meant to be paired with <a href="https://cadence-me.com">Cadence</a>, a personal behavior tracker, to increase adherence at home. Cadence schedules the behaviors you choose to repeat. When one is coming up, Cadent finds you in whichever room you are in and rolls to meet you. A line of light in its band brightens as it arrives. Then it speaks the reminder, once, and returns to its dock. You still mark it Completed or Not Completed in Cadence.</p>
    <figure class="slot" style="--ar: 9 / 16" data-label="01 Hero macro"><img src="/cadent/images/e01.jpg" alt="Cadent resting on a pale textured surface, close up." onerror="this.remove()"></figure>
    <figure class="slot" style="--ar: 2 / 3" data-label="02 Top-down, mid-roll"><img src="/cadent/images/e02.jpg" alt="Cadent from above, mid-roll across a pale floor." loading="lazy" onerror="this.remove()"></figure>
