    <p class="after-slot">Cadent is a sphere about 12 cm across. Its two hemispheres turn as wheels. They are plain bead-blasted aluminum, a matte finish that hides wear from the floor. There are no visible fasteners. A polished stainless band runs between the hemispheres, recessed below their surface. It never touches the floor. It turns on its own, independent of the wheels, to aim the camera. The band carries three things: a sapphire-covered camera that recognizes you, a slot for the line of light, and one row of speaker and microphone holes on each side of the light.</p>
